\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 2. The first-use experience: teach through doing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 The onboarding shouldn't be a slideshow explaining features. It should get the user to make their first musical discovery as quickly as possible.\
I'd make the introduction feel like a short conversation with the app.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/Tv2mJyUEj1JtapKe0klbxQtLzsKVDRLmrEymLwYzlXpzILdnCaxJor8rqijR9NbhAxH6ikX8QHbhggL7i0srvdYYJfXTCCEhPMwn3IvMeVWx8AyWElK3cRtUXyeMeValGBEwk9nE6YxsL8L5YPTOFwcxrgFv2yzK2LN-B8y6QXw?purpose=inline"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 palinoo \'96 Magische Gute-Nacht-Geschichten f\'fcr Kinder}}\
\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Step 1 \'97 Meet the companion\
A short line: \'93Sing something, play something, or let me listen.\'94\
One prominent button: Start listening. Request microphone permission only when the user chooses this action, with a clear explanation of why it's needed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/TfxHBasEOYaOu5RDCYA1ke6kRqyyOzHpSeoyuSljzFyd6kw1ytVOkbX8Z0gMiGIH6CeDZ-IGDiQeLn3ygu1nneGC86uQnWDd3dhOs6yAcXt1C3EpQOOBl6UfEHgmQMiybqDpEaMvl3PzqZj1lz99cBJ7fzO3-FeSHuPFbKBLLcw?purpose=inline"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Explore Resources | Friendly Circle Berlin}}\
\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Step 2 \'97 Make sound\
The companion becomes attentive. A live waveform or flowing line responds to the input. A small prompt says, \'93Try holding a note for a moment.\'94\
The user learns what to do by seeing the app respond, not by reading instructions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/jGQc8IvtDUi2rDtM5hw2wqfHrzjuNipYmACU21uR_2yvIDJaGW9FnxZqAw2rxPhO7hMPRBLduyZPmJGaUoEyFbzzzTn2asMfU3esJdI2vaMODajCjJSjvwVvMLpeosa-GXgIEc_3t9CYqwnPX2OZeiVB6fd4AlnpXH0K4yZSVqg?purpose=inline"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Press Kit \'96 Brand Assets & Media Resources | cori}}\
\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Step 3 \'97 Discover something\
The app identifies a note and reveals it naturally: \'93That sounds like an A.\'94\
The note appears on the visualisation, perhaps with its pitch and stability. The user can tap it to hear the note again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/LPWfUHlN_-GfCF7XEEY0eZpraCnDMZGsH5u3bC-lJ3WemO7u6E_KZyNOAwz7Vg1uGcWgdi5C_v7aTh6JWQkbJKXjOsS9jYsz7OqlDsVhV4_VNp9pL8dPy1agBpJSL1Zen1uadCqiQRKVS-cnVLUhJ6VhB6J8NKfivyVhym91qB8?purpose=inline"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 "Pastel Music Notes - Light Colors" Poster for Sale by 201farmer | Redbubble}}\
\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Step 4 \'97 Open the next door\
\'93Want to hear what goes with it?\'94\
The app offers a harmony to try. This is the moment the user discovers that it can do more than detect sound.\
The critical thing is that onboarding ends with a musical experience, not a checklist of features.\
Also, don't force every user through all four steps. Someone importing a recording should be able to get straight to analysing it, and a returning user should never have to repeat the introduction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. The listening screen: one screen, one main job\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 This is the screen I'd spend the most design effort on. It is the heart of the product.\
When listening starts, the home screen should transition into the listening experience rather than opening a completely unrelated tool.\
Listening\
Live input \'b7 C major\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
