\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Illustrative live-listening state. In a real implementation, the note display should reflect actual detection confidence and avoid presenting uncertain readings as facts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A few important design choices here:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The sound is the hero. The detected note or melody gets the most space, rather than the mascot or a collection of cards.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Visualisation has a purpose. It helps users see pitch movement and timing. It shouldn't be a random animated waveform.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Next steps are contextual. Notes and harmonies appear as the most relevant things to do with the sound, not as an entire toolbox.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recording controls stay accessible. Start, pause, and finish should be obvious without dominating the screen.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 I would not permanently display every detected note, chord, key, frequency, confidence score, and theory explanation at once. Those are layers the user can open when interested.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 4. Let each action reveal its own screen\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Instead of separate destinations for every feature, think of the app as a sequence of increasingly meaningful views.\
Listen\
Capture a sound or import a recording\
Understand\
Melody, notes, pitch and detected chords\
Experiment\
Try harmonies, transpose notes, compare sounds\
Learn\
Discover why it works and what to try next\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These are stages in a workflow, not four mandatory screens. Users can skip directly to the stage they want.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 For example, when the app detects a melody, the note display could naturally expand into a more detailed melody view. Selecting a note could reveal its frequency, playback, and context. Choosing \'93Explore harmonies\'94 could then transform the same visualisation to show possible accompanying notes.\
That continuity is important. The user should feel like they're looking more closely at the same piece of music, not switching between disconnected utilities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. The harmony experience: make it something you can play with\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 This is where I think the app can become genuinely compelling.\
Rather than showing a list of chord names and theory labels, show the original melody and let the user hear possible harmonies alongside it.\
Explore harmonies\
YOUR MELODY\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 TRY AN ACCOMPANYING LINE\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Gentle harmony\
A simple line that complements the melody\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Hear both lines together, then compare them separately.\
More movement\
Try a more active line with a different musical character.\
Keep it simple\
Explore an option with fewer note changes.\
Play both together\
The choices should be musical and understandable before they are technical. \'93Gentle harmony\'94 and \'93More movement\'94 are inviting entry points; labels such as \'93third above\'94 or \'93diatonic voice leading\'94 can be available when the user wants to learn more.\
The interaction loop is:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Choose a possibility.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hear it with the original.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compare it with another option.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adjust or keep it.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Discover why it works, if curious.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The important part is that every choice produces an audible result. The app should not make people read music theory before they can experiment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 6. The companion's personality should come from cause and effect\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 I would keep the illustrated microphone, but make it a supporting character rather than the centre of every screen.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Idle: relaxed, quietly present.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Listening: attentive, with subtle musical marks reacting to input.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Detecting a note: a small response as the note locks in.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Finding a harmony: its visual accents connect to the new musical line.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Uncertain analysis: it communicates uncertainty honestly rather than confidently inventing a result.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Playback: its movement follows the actual sound or beat, rather than running a generic loop.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The visual language should change as the user learns more. A single note might appear as a clear mark; a melody might unfold into a connected line; a harmony might appear as a second line that fits around the first.\
That gives the interface a coherent visual grammar. The music itself creates the visual experience.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 7. A few things I'd deliberately avoid\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A large dashboard full of cards, statistics, recent activity, and shortcuts.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A persistent navigation bar with a separate destination for every capability.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A mascot that takes up half the screen after the user has started working.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Decorative waveforms that look impressive but communicate nothing.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Excessive pastel panels that make every screen feel like a wellness app.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Exposing advanced theory controls before the user needs them.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Making every operation a multi-step wizard; experienced users should be able to move quickly.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The app can have depth without displaying that depth all at once.\
